[size=6][b]BetterDrone — Extended Drone Limits for StarRupture[/b][/size]

Extends building drone limits beyond the default values, and adds drone controls and tools. Fully configurable without modifying game files. All values can be edited live in game, in the BetterDrone panel or the ModLoaders F2 menu.

[b]Client-side only[/b]

[b]Open BetterDrone:[/b] press [b]Esc[/b] and pick [b]BETTER DRONE[/b] under OPTIONS, or press [b]F10[/b] (rebindable on the ModLoader config page, Controls).

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{{REPO}}/{{TAG}}/images/pause-menu.png[/img]

[quote][b]If you encounter issues or just have a question, please discuss this in our Discord which you can find on the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starrupture/mods/89]Modloaders Description Page[/url] here on Nexus.[/b][/quote]

[line]

[size=5][b]What It Does[/b][/size]

BetterDrone increases the limits of the building drone and applies your configured values automatically each time the game runs.

You can customise:

[list]
[*]Drone movement speed, acceleration, deceleration and boost
[*]Maximum horizontal range
[*]Maximum vertical range
[*]Drone Size: a smaller drone fits ladder holes and gaps, and speed doesn't change with size ✦
[*]Drone audio volumes
[*]Allows the drone in places it should not usually be called, including during wave events (Always Allow Drone)
[*][size=2]Allows the drone to interact with buildings opening their UIs like you would do normally on foot[/size]
[/list]

Warning indicators are automatically adjusted to match your configured limits.

[size=4][b]The BetterDrone panel ✦[/b][/size]

A slider, a number box and a reset arrow for each row: Drone Speed, Acceleration, Deceleration, Boost Multiplier, Max Radius, Max Height, Drone Size, plus a collapsed Audio section (Master sets the rest). [b]Esc[/b] or [b]Q[/b] closes it. Game sessions only.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{{REPO}}/{{TAG}}/images/panel.png[/img]

[list]
[*][b]Speed Display Unit[/b] — km/h (default), mph or cm/s. Sets the speed, acceleration and range rows, the toast, the speedometer and the HUD's distance and height readouts (feet with mph, metres otherwise). ✦
[*][b]Speedometer[/b] — the drone's speed under the HUD's distance readout, its number lined up with the distance digits; the HUD ring stays centred on the crosshair as the distance and height change. On by default. ✦
[*][b]Saved presets[/b] — save, rename and delete your own for speed and range. Built-in names are reserved.
[*][b]Speed presets[/b] (speed cm/s, boost, accel/decel cm/s²) — Stock game's own (400), 2x, 4000 · Better Construction 2500, 2.5x, 5000 · Agile Builder 4000, 3x, 10000 · Long Haul 5000, 3x, 12000 · Ludicrous Speed 8000, 4x, 20000
[*][b]Range presets[/b] (max radius / max height cm) — Stock game's own (4000 / 3500) · Better Construction 10000 / 5000 · Agile Builder 20000 / 10000 · Map-wide 1000000 / 500000
[/list]

Stock uses the game's own speed and range. Better Construction and Map-wide follow CrazyCovin's Better Construction Drone mod.

[size=4][b]Boost ✦[/b][/size]

Hold the boost key (your game's Sprint key by default, rebinds included; rebindable on the ModLoader config page, Controls) to multiply speed by Boost Multiplier (1 to 10x, default 2x), up to 20000 cm/s. Acceleration and deceleration ramp it on and off.

[size=4][b]Preset hotkeys and toast ✦[/b][/size]

While the drone is out, [b]-[/b] and [b]=[/b] (rebindable on the ModLoader config page, Controls) step to the next slower and faster speed preset, built-in and saved. A toast at the top right shows the name, speed and Boost speed for 1.5 s. Ignored on foot, with a menu open or with the panel open.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{{REPO}}/{{TAG}}/images/preset-toast.png[/img]

[size=4][b]Interacting from the drone[/b][/size]

Look at a building and press [b]E[/b] (rebindable on the ModLoader config page, Interaction) to open its UI, as you would on foot. Also works in delete mode, and gathers wild plants, fruit and eggs (host and single player only).

[size=4][b]The map from the drone ✦[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Open it[/b] — press [b]M[/b] (rebindable on the ModLoader config page, Interaction) while you fly. It never opens over another menu.
[*][b]Marker[/b] — the drone gets its own, a small reticle in your player-arrow colour that turns with the drone. The game's arrow stays at your parked body.
[*][b]Drone Reveals Map[/b] — off by default. Uncovers the map as you fly, at the walking radius and spacing. Saved with your game. Not inside the Forgotten Engine.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{{REPO}}/{{TAG}}/images/map-marker.png[/img]

[size=4][b]Mining from the drone ✦[/b][/size]

Hold [b]G[/b] (rebindable on the ModLoader config page, Controls) while flying to mine the ore under the crosshair: meteor ores, their chunks and infinite ore veins. Range, damage, fire rate, heat, beam and sounds follow the mining tool; yield goes to your inventory. Host and single player only.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{{REPO}}/{{TAG}}/images/laser-heat-ring.png[/img]

[list]
[*][b]Stops[/b] on release, a new or lost target, recall, an open menu or death. After a full inventory, press again.
[*][b]Heat[/b] — a ring around the crosshair fills as the laser heats, orange by 75%, red by 90%. After an overheat the laser stays locked until the heat has drained (about 97 s) or been vented.
[*][b]Vent[/b] — press your Reload key (R unless rebound) in the drone to vent the heat as the mining tool's R does: the vent takes 0.04 s per stack, plus 4 s when overheated (8 s from a full, overheated laser), the stacks coming off evenly, and the overheat ends with the last one. It does nothing with no heat or while firing, and firing stops a vent that is not overheated. The vent is silent.
[*][b]Drill[/b] — its heat is read, never changed. BetterCheats' Mining Damage, Range, Hit Rate and Overheat Cooldown rows apply.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Floor guard[/b][/size]

With the range above stock, flying far out can unload the floor under your parked character. If it falls straight down, it is held in place until the floor is back, then set down walking. Gives up after 10 s. Walking ends the hold only after 3 s, so a key held while recalling doesn't drop you. No setting.

[size=4][b]Keep area around body loaded ✦[/b][/size]

The game loads the world around the view, and in the drone the view is the drone. Fly far out and the ground around your parked character unloads, so the world is gone when you come back. While the drone is out, your character gets one of the game's own streaming sources (the kind teleporters use) with a small round shape, so the area within Body Area Radius of your body stays loaded. Default 40 m, the game's own drone range. Removed when the drone comes back, on turning it off, on death, world exit and RELOAD. Cost: memory and some actor ticks for that area, not GPU time. Setting: Keep Area Around Body Loaded (on by default), Body Area Radius.

[size=4][b]Wave shelter ✦[/b][/size]

Fly the drone outside during a wave while your character stays safe in the shelter and won't die. With Always Allow Drone off, the stock rule that ends the drone in an interior follows your character too, so flying the drone into one does not end it. No setting.

[line]

[size=5][b]Configuration[/b][/size]

Config file:
[i]"Plugins\config\BetterDrone.ini"[/i]

The file is generated on first launch. Edit it in game on the ModLoader config page (F2) and changes apply live, keys included. Hand edits to any file need a restart or RELOAD.

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/{{REPO}}/{{TAG}}/images/config-page.png[/img]

[list]
[*]Always Allow Drone — false
[*]Keep Area Around Body Loaded — true
[*]Body Area Radius — 40 (metres, 20 to 200)
[*]Interact In Drone Mode — true
[*]Interact Key — E
[*]Map In Drone Mode — true
[*]Map Key — M
[*]Drone Reveals Map — false
[*]Toggle Key — F10
[*]Boost Key — Sprint (follows your Sprint key)
[*]Previous Preset Key — Hyphen
[*]Next Preset Key — Equals
[*]Mining Laser Key — G
[/list]

Panel values are saved to [i]"Plugins\config\BetterDrone-Panel.ini"[/i], clamped to these ranges:

[list]
[*]SpeedPerSec — movement speed (1 to 20000 cm/s, default the game's own, 400)
[*]MaxRadius — horizontal range (100 to 1000000 cm, default the game's own, 4000)
[*]MaxHeight — vertical range (100 to 500000 cm, default the game's own, 3500)
[*]SphereRadius — Drone Size, collision radius (20 to 50 cm, default 50)
[*]BoostMultiplier — 1 to 10, default 2
[*]Acceleration, Deceleration — 4000 to 50000 cm/s², default 4000
[*]IdleVolume, MovementVolume, RotationVolume, StationVolume — 0 to 1, default 1
[*]SpeedUnit — km/h, mph or cm/s
[/list]

Saved presets are in [i]"Plugins\config\BetterDrone-Presets.ini"[/i]. Values in an older BetterDrone.ini move over on first run.

All values persist between game restarts.

[line]

[size=5][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Download the latest file from the [b]Files[/b] tab
[*]Open the ZIP file
[*]Copy the contents of the included Plugins folder into:
[i]"StarRupture\Binaries\Win64\ModLoader\Plugins"[/i]
[*]Launch the game once to generate the config file
[*]Set your values in the BetterDrone panel (or edit the INI files above)
[/list]

Requires [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starrupture/mods/89]AlienX's Mod Loader[/url], v1.23.0 or later (plugin interface v74).

[line]

[size=5][b]Troubleshooting[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Values not changing[/b] — check [i]"ModLoader.log in Binaries\Win64\ModLoader\Logs\"[/i] for errors
[*][b]Plugin not loading[/b] — ensure ModLoader is installed and the plugin is in the Plugins folder
[*][b]Mining laser does nothing[/b] — drone mode, host or single player only. Full inventory: press again. Overheated: wait for the ring to clear
[/list]

